  "description": "JODNIB crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H51 Gd4 N16 O23 1+,C1 H4 O1,4(C2 H3 N1),N1 O3 1-,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.574-5.507 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.24-174.99°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C61H67Gd4N21O29. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
